---@class infisical.AttachKubernetesAuthRequest
---@field identityId string The ID of the machine identity to attach the configuration onto.
---@field templateId? string The ID of the Kubernetes auth template to source connection settings from. When provided, the host, CA certificate, token reviewer JWT, token review mode, gateway, and allowed audience are taken from the template and cannot be set individually.
---@field kubernetesHost? string|distilled.Null The host string, host:port pair, or URL to the base of the Kubernetes API server.
---@field caCert? string The PEM-encoded CA certificate used to validate the Kubernetes API server's TLS certificate. Required when verifyTlsCertificate is true. Supplying a non-empty caCert always implies verifyTlsCertificate=true; explicitly setting the toggle to false in the same request is rejected.
---@field verifyTlsCertificate? boolean Whether to verify the Kubernetes API server's TLS certificate against the configured CA certificate. When true, caCert is required. When false, the connection is still over HTTPS but the API server's certificate is not verified, and caCert must be empty. If omitted, defaults to true when caCert is provided and false otherwise.
---@field tokenReviewerJwt? string Optional JWT token for accessing Kubernetes TokenReview API. If provided, this long-lived token will be used to validate service account tokens during authentication. If omitted, the client's own JWT will be used instead, which requires the client to have the system:auth-delegator ClusterRole binding.
---@field tokenReviewMode? infisical.AttachKubernetesAuthRequestTokenReviewMode|string The mode to use for token review. Must be one of: 'api', 'gateway'. Defaults to 'api' when omitted. If gateway is selected, the gateway must be deployed in Kubernetes, and the gateway must have the system:auth-delegator ClusterRole binding.
---@field allowedNamespaces string The comma-separated list of trusted namespaces that service accounts must belong to authenticate with Infisical.
---@field allowedNames string The comma-separated list of trusted service account names that can authenticate with Infisical.
---@field allowedAudience? string The optional audience claim that the service account JWT token must have to authenticate with Infisical.
---@field gatewayId? string|distilled.Null The ID of the gateway to use when performing kubernetes API requests.
---@field gatewayPoolId? string|distilled.Null
---@field accessTokenTrustedIps? infisical.AttachKubernetesAuthRequestAccessTokenTrustedIpsList The IPs or CIDR ranges that access tokens can be used from.
---@field accessTokenTTL? number The lifetime for an access token in seconds.
---@field accessTokenMaxTTL? number The maximum lifetime for an access token in seconds.
---@field accessTokenNumUsesLimit? number The maximum number of times that an access token can be used.

