---@field configuration infisical.CreateInternalCertificateAuthorityV1RequestConfiguration

---@class infisical.CreateInternalCertificateAuthorityV1RequestConfiguration
---@field type infisical.CreateInternalCertificateAuthorityV1RequestConfigurationType|string The type of CA to create.
---@field friendlyName? string A friendly name for the CA.
---@field commonName? string The common name (CN) for the CA.
---@field organization? string The organization (O) for the CA.
---@field ou? string The organization unit (OU) for the CA.
---@field country? string The country name (C) for the CA.
---@field province? string The state of province name for the CA.
---@field locality? string The locality name for the CA.
---@field notBefore? string The date and time when the CA becomes valid in YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sssZ format.
---@field notAfter? string The date and time when the CA expires in YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sssZ format.
---@field maxPathLength? number|distilled.Null The maximum number of intermediate CAs that may follow this CA in the certificate / CA chain. A maxPathLength of -1 implies no path limit on the chain.
---@field keyAlgorithm infisical.CreateInternalCertificateAuthorityV1RequestConfigurationKeyAlgorithm|string The type of public key algorithm and size, in bits, of the key pair for the CA; when you create an intermediate CA, you must use a key algorithm supported by the parent CA.
---@field keySource? infisical.CreateInternalCertificateAuthorityV1RequestConfigurationKeySource|string Where the CA's signing key is generated and stored. 'infisical' keeps the key in Infisical's KMS; 'hsm' generates and stores the key in the HSM reached through the specified HSM Connector; 'aws-kms' generates the key in AWS KMS through the specified AWS connection, and every signature is made by AWS KMS.
---@field hsmConnectorId? string The ID of the HSM Connector to generate and store the CA's signing key in. Required when keySource is 'hsm'.
