---@class infisical.CreateLdapConfigRequest
---@field organizationId string The ID of the organization to create the LDAP config for.
---@field isActive boolean Whether to enable or disable this LDAP configuration.
---@field url string The LDAP server to connect to such as `ldap://ldap.your-org.com`, `ldaps://ldap.myorg.com:636` (for connection over SSL/TLS), etc.
---@field bindDN string The distinguished name of the object to bind when performing the user search such as `cn=infisical,ou=Users,dc=acme,dc=com`
---@field bindPass string The password to use along with Bind DN when performing the user search.
---@field uniqueUserAttribute? string The attribute to use as the unique identifier of LDAP users such as `sAMAccountName`, `cn`, `uid`, `objectGUID`. If left blank, defaults to uidNumber
---@field searchBase string The base DN to use for the user search such as `ou=Users,dc=acme,dc=com`
---@field searchFilter? string The template used to construct the LDAP user search filter such as `(uid={{username}})` uses literal `{{username}}` to have the given username used in the search. The default is `(uid={{username}})` which is compatible with several common directory schemas.
---@field groupSearchBase string LDAP search base to use for group membership search such as `ou=Groups,dc=acme,dc=com`
---@field groupSearchFilter? string The template used when constructing the group membership query such as `(&(objectClass=posixGroup)(memberUid={{.Username}}))`. The template can access the following context variables: `[UserDN, UserName]`. The default is `(|(memberUid={{.Username}})(member={{.UserDN}})(uniqueMember={{.UserDN}}))` which is compatible with several common directory schemas.
---@field caCert? string The CA certificate to use when verifying the LDAP server certificate.
---@field clientCertificate? string PEM-encoded client certificate presented during the TLS handshake for mutual TLS (mTLS). Must be provided together with clientKeyCertificate.
---@field clientKeyCertificate? string PEM-encoded private key matching the client certificate, used during the TLS handshake for mutual TLS (mTLS). Must be provided together with clientCertificate.

