---@class infisical.ImportCaCrossSignedCertificateRequest
---@field caId string The ID of the CA to import the cross-signed certificate for.
---@field certificate string The PEM-encoded cross-signed certificate: the CA's certificate signed by the old CA as a CA certificate. It must have the same subject, public key, and subject key identifier as the CA.
---@field certificateChain string The PEM-encoded certificates of the old CA, in order: start with the CA that signed the cross-signed certificate and end with its root. When the old root signed it directly, this is the old root's certificate.

---@class infisical.ImportCaCrossSignedCertificateResponse
---@field crossSignedCertificate infisical.ImportCaCrossSignedCertificateResponseCrossSignedCertificate

---@class infisical.ImportCaCrossSignedCertificateResponseCrossSignedCertificate
---@field caId string The ID of the CA the cross-signed certificate belongs to.
---@field certificate string The PEM-encoded cross-signed certificate.
---@field certificateChain string The PEM-encoded certificates of the old CA, from the one that signed the cross-signed certificate up to its root.
---@field issuer string The distinguished name of the CA that signed the cross-signed certificate.
---@field serialNumber string The serial number of the cross-signed certificate.
---@field notBefore string The date and time the cross-signed certificate becomes valid.
---@field notAfter string The date and time the cross-signed certificate expires. After this, new certificates no longer include it in their chain.

