---@class infisical.ListOrganizationAuditLogsRequest
---@field projectId? string Optionally filter logs by project ID. If not provided, logs from the entire organization will be returned.
---@field environment? string The environment to filter logs by. If not provided, logs from all environments will be returned. Note that the projectId parameter must also be provided.
---@field actorType? infisical.ListOrganizationAuditLogsRequestActorType|string The type of actor to filter audit logs by. Must be provided when the actor parameter targets a non-user actor type (e.g. identity, kmipClient).
---@field secretPath? string The path of the secret to query audit logs for. Note that the projectId parameter must also be provided.
---@field secretKey? string The key of the secret to query audit logs for. Note that the projectId parameter must also be provided.
---@field eventType? any
---@field eventClass? any Filter by event class, comma-separated for multiple values (management, authentication, authorization, data-access). Combined with eventType, only event types in both are returned. If the selected classes include secret events, the environment, secretPath, and secretKey filters drop every event whose metadata doesn't match, including events that aren't about secrets. If they don't, those filters are ignored.
---@field userAgentType? infisical.ListOrganizationAuditLogsRequestUserAgentType|string Choose which consuming application to export audit logs for.
---@field eventMetadata? string Filter by event metadata key-value pairs. Formatted as `key1=value1,key2=value2`, with comma-separation.
---@field startDate? string The date to start the export from.
---@field endDate? string The date to end the export at.
---@field offset? number The offset to start from. If you enter 10, it will start from the 10th audit log.
---@field limit? number The number of audit logs to return.
---@field actor? string The ID of a specific actor to filter audit logs by. For user actors this is the userId; for identity actors this is the identityId. When filtering non-user actor types, the actorType parameter must also be provided.

---@alias infisical.ListOrganizationAuditLogsRequestActorType "platform"|"kmipClient"|"user"|"service"|"identity"|"scimClient"|"acmeProfile"|"acmeAccount"|"estAccount"|"scepAccount"|"unknownUser"|"gateway"|"relay"|"kmipServer"|"agentVaultProxy"

---@alias infisical.ListOrganizationAuditLogsRequestUserAgentType "web"|"cli"|"k8-operator"|"terraform"|"other"|"InfisicalPythonSDK"|"InfisicalNodeSDK"

