---@class infisical.UpdateKubernetesAuthRequest
---@field identityId string The ID of the machine identity to update the auth method for.
---@field templateId? string|distilled.Null The ID of the Kubernetes auth template to link. While linked, connection settings are managed by the template and cannot be set individually. Pass null to unlink the template; the settings copied from it are kept.
---@field kubernetesHost? string|distilled.Null The new host string, host:port pair, or URL to the base of the Kubernetes API server.
---@field caCert? string The new PEM-encoded CA certificate used to validate the Kubernetes API server's TLS certificate. Required when verifyTlsCertificate is true. Supplying a non-empty caCert always implies verifyTlsCertificate=true; the update is rejected if the resulting effective state would store a CA together with verifyTlsCertificate=false.
---@field verifyTlsCertificate? boolean Whether to verify the Kubernetes API server's TLS certificate against the configured CA certificate. When true, caCert is required. When false, the connection is still over HTTPS but the API server's certificate is not verified, and the resulting effective CA must be empty. If omitted while supplying a non-empty caCert in the same update, the toggle is auto-promoted to true; otherwise the stored value is preserved.
---@field tokenReviewerJwt? string|distilled.Null Optional JWT token for accessing Kubernetes TokenReview API. If provided, this long-lived token replaces the stored one and is used to validate service account tokens during authentication. Omit it, or send an empty string, to keep the stored JWT. Set it to null to remove the stored JWT; the client's own JWT is then used instead, which requires the client to have the system:auth-delegator ClusterRole binding. A stored JWT cannot be read back, so it must be supplied again when changing the host, gateway, gateway pool, CA certificate, or TLS verification.
---@field tokenReviewMode? infisical.UpdateKubernetesAuthRequestTokenReviewMode|string The mode to use for token review. Must be one of: 'api', 'gateway'. If gateway is selected, the gateway must be deployed in Kubernetes, and the gateway must have the system:auth-delegator ClusterRole binding.
---@field allowedNamespaces? string The new comma-separated list of trusted namespaces that service accounts must belong to authenticate with Infisical.
---@field allowedNames? string The new comma-separated list of trusted service account names that can authenticate with Infisical.
---@field allowedAudience? string The new optional audience claim that the service account JWT token must have to authenticate with Infisical.
---@field gatewayId? string|distilled.Null The ID of the gateway to use when performing kubernetes API requests.
---@field gatewayPoolId? string|distilled.Null
---@field accessTokenTrustedIps? infisical.UpdateKubernetesAuthRequestAccessTokenTrustedIpsList The new IPs or CIDR ranges that access tokens can be used from.
---@field accessTokenTTL? number The new lifetime for an acccess token in seconds.
---@field accessTokenNumUsesLimit? number The new maximum number of times that an access token can be used.
---@field accessTokenMaxTTL? number The new maximum lifetime for an acccess token in seconds.

---@class infisical.UpdateKubernetesAuthRequestAccessTokenTrustedIpsItem
---@field ipAddress string

