---@class infisical.UpdatePkiCaInternalResponseConfiguration
---@field type infisical.UpdatePkiCaInternalResponseConfigurationType The type of CA to create.
---@field friendlyName? string A friendly name for the CA.
---@field commonName? string The common name (CN) for the CA.
---@field organization? string The organization (O) for the CA.
---@field ou? string The organization unit (OU) for the CA.
---@field country? string The country name (C) for the CA.
---@field province? string The state of province name for the CA.
---@field locality? string The locality name for the CA.
---@field notBefore? string The date and time when the CA becomes valid in YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sssZ format.
---@field notAfter? string The date and time when the CA expires in YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sssZ format.
---@field maxPathLength? number|distilled.Null The maximum number of intermediate CAs that may follow this CA in the certificate / CA chain. A maxPathLength of -1 implies no path limit on the chain.
---@field keyAlgorithm infisical.UpdatePkiCaInternalResponseConfigurationKeyAlgorithm The type of public key algorithm and size, in bits, of the key pair for the CA; when you create an intermediate CA, you must use a key algorithm supported by the parent CA.
---@field keySource? infisical.UpdatePkiCaInternalResponseConfigurationKeySource Where the CA's signing key is generated and stored. 'infisical' keeps the key in Infisical's KMS; 'hsm' generates and stores the key in the HSM reached through the specified HSM Connector; 'aws-kms' generates the key in AWS KMS through the specified AWS connection, and every signature is made by AWS KMS.
---@field hsmConnectorId? string The ID of the HSM Connector to generate and store the CA's signing key in. Required when keySource is 'hsm'.
---@field hsmKeyLabel? string Deprecated: use externalKeyId, which holds the same key label for HSM-backed CAs. The label of the CA's signing key on the HSM.
---@field appConnectionId? string The ID of the AWS connection used to create the CA's signing key in AWS KMS and to sign with it. Required when keySource is 'aws-kms'.
---@field appConnectionName? string The name of the AWS connection the CA's signing key is reached through. Not user-supplied.
---@field hsmConnectorName? string The name of the HSM Connector the CA's signing key is reached through. Not user-supplied.
---@field region? infisical.UpdatePkiCaInternalResponseConfigurationRegion The AWS region the CA's signing key is created in. Required when keySource is 'aws-kms', and returned when reading the CA.
---@field externalKeyId? string The identifier of the CA's signing key in its key source: the key ARN for AWS KMS, or the key label for HSM. Not user-supplied: the key is created when the CA is created.
---@field dn? string|distilled.Null
---@field parentCaId? string|distilled.Null
---@field serialNumber? string|distilled.Null
---@field activeCaCertId? string|distilled.Null
---@field crlDistributionPointUrls? infisical.UpdatePkiCaInternalResponseConfigurationCrlDistributionPointUrlsList Additional CRL Distribution Point URLs (HTTP/HTTPS) embedded in every certificate issued by this CA. Up to 4 URLs; the Infisical-managed CRL endpoint is included by default unless disabled.
---@field disableManagedCrlDistributionPointUrl? boolean When set to true, the Infisical-managed CRL endpoint URL will not be embedded in certificates issued by this CA. Only custom CRL Distribution Point URLs (if any) will be included.
---@field isOcspEnabled? boolean When set to true, certificates issued by this CA carry the Infisical-managed OCSP responder URL in their Authority Information Access extension, and that responder answers revocation status queries for them. Applies to certificates issued after it is enabled.

---Additional CRL Distribution Point URLs (HTTP/HTTPS) embedded in every certificate issued by this CA. Up to 4 URLs; the Infisical-managed CRL endpoint is included by default unless disabled.
