---@class infisical.UpdateProxiedServiceRequest
---@field serviceId string The ID of the proxied service to update.
---@field name? string The new name of the proxied service.
---@field hostPattern? string The new comma-separated host patterns.
---@field isEnabled? boolean Whether the proxied service is enabled. The agent proxy skips disabled services.
---@field credentials? infisical.UpdateProxiedServiceRequestCredentialsList The new credentials. When provided, the entire credentials collection is replaced; when omitted, existing credentials are left unchanged.

---@class infisical.UpdateProxiedServiceRequestCredentialsItem
---@field secretKey? string|distilled.Secret The key name of the referenced static secret. The secret must live in the same folder as the service. Provide exactly one of secretKey or dynamicSecretName.
---@field dynamicSecretName? string The name of the referenced dynamic secret. The dynamic secret must live in the same folder as the service; the agent proxy mints a lease and injects a field from its output. Provide exactly one of secretKey or dynamicSecretName. Referenced by name (like secretKey), so a deleted-then-recreated dynamic secret with the same name re-links automatically.
---@field dynamicSecretField? string For a dynamic secret credential: which lease output field to inject (e.g. 'DB_PASSWORD', 'TOKEN'). Must be a valid output field for the dynamic secret's provider type.
---@field role infisical.UpdateProxiedServiceRequestCredentialsItemRole|string How the credential is applied: 'header-rewrite' sets an HTTP header on the outbound request; 'credential-substitution' replaces a placeholder value in the request.
---@field headerName? string For header rewriting: the header to set, e.g. 'Authorization' or 'x-api-key'.
---@field headerPrefix? string For header rewriting: an optional prefix joined to the secret value with a space, e.g. 'Bearer'.
---@field headerPurpose? infisical.UpdateProxiedServiceRequestCredentialsItemHeaderPurpose|string For HTTP basic auth: 'username' or 'password'. The agent proxy combines the pair into a single 'Authorization: Basic' header. Cannot be combined with headerName or headerPrefix.
---@field placeholderKey? string For credential substitution: the environment variable name the agent receives.
---@field placeholderValue? string For credential substitution: the placeholder value the agent proxy swaps for the real secret value on the wire.
---@field substitutionSurfaces? infisical.UpdateProxiedServiceRequestCredentialsItemSubstitutionSurfacesList For credential substitution: which request surfaces are scanned for the placeholder. Allowed values: 'header', 'path', 'query', 'body'.

---For HTTP basic auth: 'username' or 'password'. The agent proxy combines the pair into a single 'Authorization: Basic' header. Cannot be combined with headerName or headerPrefix.
---@alias infisical.UpdateProxiedServiceRequestCredentialsItemHeaderPurpose "username"|"password"

---How the credential is applied: 'header-rewrite' sets an HTTP header on the outbound request; 'credential-substitution' replaces a placeholder value in the request.
