---@class infisical.UpdateTlsCertAuthRequest
---@field identityId string The ID of the machine identity to update the auth method for.
---@field caCertificate? string The PEM-encoded CA certificate to validate client certificates.
---@field verifyClientCertificateChain? boolean When false (default), the CA certificate must be the direct issuer of the client's leaf certificate. When true, the CA certificate is treated as a trust anchor and the client-presented chain (leaf plus intermediates) is validated up to it, supporting issuers that rotate beneath a stable root such as SPIRE X.509-SVIDs.
---@field bindAccessTokenToCertificate? boolean When true, access tokens issued by this auth method only work on requests that present the same client certificate used to log in. Turning this on revokes the identity's existing TLS Certificate Auth access tokens.
---@field allowedCommonNames? string|distilled.Null The comma-separated list of trusted common names that are allowed to authenticate with Infisical.
---@field allowedSubjectAltNames? infisical.UpdateTlsCertAuthRequestAllowedSubjectAltNamesList|distilled.Null The comma-separated list of trusted subject alternative names that are allowed to authenticate with Infisical. Prefix entries by type (URI:, DNS:, IP:, EMAIL:). Bare entries are treated as DNS names.
---@field accessTokenTrustedIps? infisical.UpdateTlsCertAuthRequestAccessTokenTrustedIpsList The new IPs or CIDR ranges that access tokens can be used from.
---@field accessTokenTTL? number The new lifetime for an access token in seconds.
---@field accessTokenNumUsesLimit? number The new maximum number of times that an access token can be used.
---@field accessTokenMaxTTL? number The new maximum lifetime for an access token in seconds.

